  "dom_id": "step-q113628",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "${(1+\\frac{c}{3})}^{6}=$",
  "worked_solution": "The first three terms of the binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+\u22ef.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=\\frac{c}{3}$ and $n=6$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1+\\frac{c}{3})}^{6} & =1+6\\cdot \\frac{c}{3}+\\frac{6(6-1)}{2!}\\cdot {(\\frac{c}{3})}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1+2c+\\frac{6\\cdot 5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{c}^{2}}{9}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1+2c+15\\cdot \\frac{{c}^{2}}{9}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1+2c+\\frac{5{c}^{2}}{3}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
